<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">interrupts</ansi>

A spell takes time: its caster <ansi fg="yellow">chants</ansi> for a round or two before it goes
off (<ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>). A chant is fragile. <ansi fg="yellow">Any weapon blow that draws blood
breaks it</ansi>, however light:

  <ansi fg="command">The goblin hexer's chant breaks off under the blow. (Withering Hex interrupted)</ansi>

A melee blow, a sling stone, or an arrow breaks it, and so does a blow
you take in someone else's place (guarding them, or catching it in the
front row). A miss, a dodged blow, a hit that does no damage, bleeding or
burning, and a spell do not.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When your chant breaks</ansi>

- The spell is lost, and <ansi fg="yellow">half its mana comes back</ansi> (rounded down):
  <ansi fg="command">The blow breaks your chant, and Minor Heal is lost. (Minor Heal interrupted, 1 mana back)</ansi>
- The same goes for your companions. A healer or caster tries again at its
  next chance, as its strategy says (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When a foe's chant breaks</ansi>

- An enemy caster, such as the <ansi fg="yellow">goblin hexer</ansi> of the Dark Forest, starts
  the chant again from the first word at its next turn. It spends no more
  mana, but must chant the whole spell again, and every blow that draws
  blood breaks it again.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Keeping your casters chanting</ansi>

- Put healers and casters in the <ansi fg="yellow">back row</ansi>, where most foes' blows can't
  reach them (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>).
- Give them a <ansi fg="yellow">guardian</ansi>: a guarded blow lands on the guardian instead
  (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>).
- Break the enemy's chants: the <ansi fg="command">casters</ansi> focus turns your whole company on
  foes that chant (<ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>). A foe chanting from its back row can
  still be reached with a bow or sling.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Shield counters</ansi>

When a melee blow misses someone holding a <ansi fg="yellow">shield</ansi>, they may slam it back
into the attacker:

  <ansi fg="command">Tamsin Reed turns the blow and drives her shield into the bandit captain. (shield bash, 3 damage, stunned)</ansi>

- A miss or a dodge gives a <ansi fg="yellow">50%</ansi> chance. The bash does <ansi fg="yellow">1 to 4 damage</ansi>, and
  one bash in four also <ansi fg="yellow">stuns</ansi> the attacker (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>).
- At most <ansi fg="yellow">one counter a round</ansi> for each shield-bearer.
- No counter against a bow or sling, and none while the bearer is knocked
  down, stunned, or chanting.
- It works both ways: a foe with a shield counters you. You choose nothing;
  holding a shield is enough.

The battle summary lists the chants each side broke (<ansi fg="command">help battle-summary</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>.
